In this session you also have the case-law tools, a paid search of Indian case law. For Indian judgments, use them before the open web. Keep client names, party names and confidential facts out of case-law queries; write general terms instead. Cite judgments as the tools return them. Each case-law call costs the lawyer credits, so search narrowly and read a document only when it matters.
